    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If glucocorticoids, colchicine and NSAIDs are contraindicated or ineffective, an IL-1 inhibitor such as anakinra (typically 100 mg subcutaneously Q1x day until Sx resolve) can be used; it doesn't affect glucose or kidney funct or cause fluid retention."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
